  "selectedReplayRule": "Current required authorization precedes replay; exact authorized retries resolve the original accepted result using the selected logical identity and immutable actor/intent/source binding. Fresh mutable feasibility, clock selection and body preparation cannot replace that original result. Expected revision is concurrency precondition, not a new identity.",
  "productRules": [
    {
      "id": "D16-07",
      "doc": "m0-d16-evidence-handling.md",
      "rule": "An evidence artifact is eligible for disposition only when its retention period has elapsed and it has no active hold."
    },
    {
      "id": "D16-08",
      "doc": "m0-d16-evidence-handling.md",
      "rule": "Disposition of evidence requires Org Admin approval recorded as an immutable decision, may be batched, and leaves a tombstone with content hash, size, retention basis, and the decision; nothing is disposed of automatically."
    },
    {
      "id": "D16-15",
      "doc": "m0-d16-evidence-handling.md",
      "rule": "When a client offboards, active holds block disposition of held artifacts; everything else follows the retention schedule after the ClientExport is delivered."
    }
  ],
  "decides": "Approval requires an Org Admin actor and a bounded rationale recorded as an immutable decision; approvals may be batched across artifacts, and nothing is disposed of automatically. Disposition leaves a tombstone carrying content hash, size, retention basis and the approving decision. An active hold on a held artifact blocks disposition during client offboarding, and all other artifacts follow the retention schedule once the ClientExport is delivered.",
